Step 2 — Push the new eas.json to GitHub
The file I just created exists in Emergent, but it's not in your Antarachavez/TrueRights repo yet. You need to push it.
Two ways:
Option A (Emergent push): Go back to Emergent → click "Save to GitHub" → push to Antarachavez/TrueRights. The eas.json will go up with the rest.
Option B (Manual, fastest): Directly in GitHub:
Go to github.com/Antarachavez/TrueRights/tree/main/frontend
Click "Add file" → "Create new file"
Name it eas.json
Paste this content:
{
  "cli": {
    "version": ">= 13.0.0",
    "appVersionSource": "remote"
  },
  "build": {
    "development": {
      "developmentClient": true,
      "distribution": "internal",
      "ios": { "simulator": true }
    },
    "preview": {
      "distribution": "internal",
      "android": { "buildType": "apk" }
    },
    "production": {
      "autoIncrement": true
    }
  },
  "submit": {
    "production": {}
  }
}
